# {{projectName}}

<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
A full-stack application with a React/TypeScript frontend and <!-- IF language=kotlin -->Kotlin<!-- END language --><!-- IF language=java -->Java<!-- END language -->/Spring Boot backend. A single `mvn package` produces a fat JAR that serves both the API and the SPA.
<!-- END stack -->
<!-- IF stack=backend-only -->
A <!-- IF language=kotlin -->Kotlin<!-- END language --><!-- IF language=java -->Java<!-- END language -->/Spring Boot backend service. `mvn package` produces a runnable JAR.
<!-- END stack -->

Built on the [Trustworks Essentials](https://github.com/trustworksdk/essentials-project) framework.

## Architecture

<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
```
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
-----------------
Browser :5173  -->  Vite Dev Server (HMR)  -->  /api/*  -->  Spring Boot :8080

PRODUCTION
----------
Browser  -->  Spring Boot :8080  -->  /api/*   (API)
                                 -->  /*       (SPA static files)
                                 -->  /swagger-ui.html (API docs)
```
<!-- END stack -->
<!-- IF stack=backend-only -->
```
Browser / Client  -->  Spring Boot :8080  -->  /api/*       (API)
                                          -->  /v3/api-docs (OpenAPI spec)
                                          -->  /swagger-ui  (interactive docs)
                                          -->  /actuator    (health/metrics)
```
<!-- END stack -->

This project follows **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)** with **CQRS** (Command Query Responsibility Segregation).

## Project Structure

```
{{artifactId}}/
├── pom.xml                        # Maven parent POM (reactor build)
├── dev.sh                         # Development convenience script
<!-- IF docker-compose -->
├── docker-compose.yml             # Database + app services
<!-- END docker-compose -->
│
├── backend/                       # Spring Boot API
│   ├── pom.xml                    # Backend module POM
│   └── src/main/{{sourceLang}}/{{packageDir}}/
│       ├── web/                   # CORS, OpenAPI, SPA filter
│       └── domains/               # Domain slices (add as you go)
<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
│
├── frontend/                      # React/TypeScript SPA
│   ├── orval.config.ts            # OpenAPI → TypeScript codegen
│   └── src/
│       ├── app/                   # App shell, routing
│       ├── shared/                # Shared components, API client
│       │   └── api/               # Generated API client (Orval)
│       └── domains/               # Domain-specific UI
│
└── contracts/                     # API contracts (generated)
    └── openapi.json               # OpenAPI spec (auto-generated)
<!-- END stack -->
```

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Java at the `java.version` in the project's POM, or newer
- Maven 3.9+
<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
- Node.js 25+
<!-- END stack -->
<!-- IF docker-compose -->
- Docker & Docker Compose
<!-- END docker-compose -->

### Run

```bash
<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
./dev.sh              # backend + frontend together
./dev.sh backend      # backend only on :8080
./dev.sh frontend     # vite dev server on :5173
./dev.sh generate     # regenerate TypeScript client from OpenAPI
<!-- END stack -->
<!-- IF stack=backend-only -->
./dev.sh backend      # backend on :8080
<!-- END stack -->
```

### Build

```bash
mvn package                    # full build
<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
mvn package -Pskip-frontend    # backend-only (no Node/npm)
<!-- END stack -->
```

### Test

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw test                                                                          # unit tests
<!-- IF stack=full-stack -->
./mvnw verify -Pskip-frontend                                                        # unit + integration
./mvnw failsafe:integration-test -Pskip-frontend -Dit.test=ChangedIT                 # single IT class (inner-loop)
<!-- END stack -->
<!-- IF stack=backend-only -->
./mvnw verify                                                                        # unit + integration
./mvnw failsafe:integration-test -Dit.test=ChangedIT                                 # single IT class (inner-loop)
<!-- END stack -->
```

For a fast inner loop, see `CLAUDE.md` → "Inner-loop integration tests".

## Working with Claude Code

`CLAUDE.md` in this repo tells Claude Code to use the **`essentials` plugin's `essentials-docs` skill** for any framework questions. The skill auto-loads on Essentials-related queries and on code signals (imports, type names) and proactively consults the plugin's design guide before editing code.

If the plugin isn't installed yet:

```
/plugin marketplace add trustworksdk/essentials-project
/plugin install essentials@essentials-marketplace
```

